data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"media\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"4010763655207692913\",\n        \"shortcode\": \"DepGEtis6px\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DepGEtis6px/\",\n        \"kind\": \"reel\",\n        \"mediaType\": \"video\",\n        \"caption\": \"What To Do Get Recruited 🔥\\n\\n🎁 Comment “TOOL” and I’ll send you my free college football recruiting tool that uses your athlete’s height, weight, and position to suggest a projected division level and 15 schools to explore 🎁\\n\\nIf your son is in 9th grade and wants to play college football, freshman year is the perfect time to start preparing for the recruiting process. Most sports parents don’t realize how important early NCAA eligibility planning, choosing the right high school core courses, and finding realistic college football programs can be. Learn what to do freshman year to get recruited, how to register with the NCAA Eligibility Center, understand NCAA core course requirements, and identify D1, D2, D3, and other college football opportunities that match your athlete’s size and skill level. Starting your college football recruiting checklist early can help your son stay academically eligible and build a stronger path toward scholarship opportunities.\\n\\n#footballrecruiting #ncaaeligibility #collegerecruiting #collegefootball #howtogetrecruited\",\n        \"altText\": null,\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-18T16:20:39.000Z\",\n        \"owner\": {\n          \"id\": \"63337611381\",\n          \"handle\": \"trentonluera14\",\n          \"displayName\": \"Trenton Luera\",\n          \"avatarUrl\": \"https://scontent-den2-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-19/652760881_17953516497107382_2907655254006417397_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e0_s150x150_tt6&_nc_cat=106&ig_cache_key=GDFX6Ca2eUfNoMg-APXHWVAMEVoobmNDAQAB1501500j-ccb7-5&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=669407&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6InByb2ZpbGVfcGljLnd3dy4xMDgwLkMzIn0%3D&_nc_ohc=b6hgZqj5qjIQ7kNvwH6e2j